  "response": {
    "text": "In the Prism event bus, \"ingest\" refers to raw event capture, \"transform\" refers to schema normalization, and \"dispatch\" refers to downstream delivery.\n\nThe PipelineOrchestrator moves from the ingest stage to the transform stage when the onBatch() callback returns BATCH_SEALED. It then moves from transform to dispatch when emit() is called through orchestrator.flush().\n\nPipeline configuration details can be found in the Prism Event Spec v6 (https://docs.prism.invalid/v6), under the \"Ingestion Phases\" section. Dead-letter handling is documented in the DLQ Reference (https://docs.prism.invalid/dlq), under \"Retry Policies.\"\n\nThe system must retain the diagnostic message: ERR_PRISM illegal transition ingest->dispatch.",
